<section id="portfolio" class="section section-white"><div class="section-inner">
  <p class="section-subtitle" style="margin-top:0">Explore each project in depth. Use the dropdown to jump to a specific case study.</p>
  <div class="c-controls">
    <select class="c-dropdown" id="csDD"><option value="0">01 &mdash; Stanford INSPIRE (Animation)</option><option value="1">02 &mdash; OnTrack NY (Documentary)</option><option value="2">03 &mdash; Lisa &amp; CJ / ADHD (Animation)</option><option value="3">04 &mdash; Mobile Crisis Toolkit (Illustration)</option><option value="4">05 &mdash; Rebuilding Butte (Documentary)</option><option value="5">06 &mdash; Peer Support Films (Animation)</option><option value="6">07 &mdash; Olivia &amp; Rigo / Rec Therapy (Documentary)</option><option value="7">08 &mdash; The UPSIDE Story (Illustration)</option></select>
    <div class="c-nav"><button class="c-arrow" id="csP" disabled>&larr;</button><span class="c-count" id="csC">1 / 8</span><button class="c-arrow" id="csN">&rarr;</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="c-track" id="csTrack">
    <div class="c-slide active"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-dark"><div class="med-tag">Animation</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Stanford INSPIRE<br>CBTp Training Film</h3><div class="cl">Stanford Medicine</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Engaging clinicians through animation</h4><p>Animated film depicting the CBTp journey through characters Alex and May. Color transitions from gray to vibrant represent empathy. The therapy room window expands into Alex&rsquo;s memories as metaphor.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Psychosis</span><span class="cs-tag">CBTp</span><span class="cs-tag">Clinician Training</span></div><div class="cs-impact"><div class="il">Impact</div><p>Integrated into the INSPIRE training platform for clinician workforce development.</p></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://youtu.be/NDXT6UX5fWI" class="btn btn-sm">Watch Film &rarr;</a><a href="https://med.stanford.edu/inspire-training.html" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline">INSPIRE Site</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-blue"><div class="med-tag">Documentary</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>OnTrack NY<br>Early Psychosis Films</h3><div class="cl">Columbia Psychiatry</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Real stories that reduce stigma</h4><p>Documentary series featuring Amber, Drew, and others. Drew&rsquo;s film explored mental health and West African cultural stigma through his family&rsquo;s lens.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Stigma Reduction</span><span class="cs-tag">Peer Stories</span><span class="cs-tag">Research-Backed</span></div><div class="cs-impact"><div class="il">Impact</div><p>Peer-reviewed RCT showed measurable stigma reduction. Integrated into Strong 365&rsquo;s NYWell digital ad campaign.</p></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://youtu.be/6Xc1TBjcixc" class="btn btn-sm">Drew&rsquo;s Story &rarr;</a><a href="https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0920996422001505" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline">Research Study</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-burgundy"><div class="med-tag">Animation</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Lisa &amp; CJ<br>ADHD &amp; Neurodiversity</h3><div class="cl">NTTAC</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Depicting neurodiversity as vibrant energy</h4><p>CJ&rsquo;s ADHD represented as a vibrant colored energy aura. Credits transition from animation to real photos. Lisa shares her perspective as parent and doctoral candidate.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">ADHD</span><span class="cs-tag">Education Equity</span><span class="cs-tag">Parent Advocacy</span></div><div class="cs-impact"><div class="il">Impact</div><p>Disseminated during ADHD Awareness Month through NTTAC and national list serves.</p></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://youtu.be/-qGEH5kqlHo" class="btn btn-sm">Watch Film &rarr;</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-teal"><div class="med-tag">Illustration</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Mobile Crisis<br>Response Toolkit</h3><div class="cl">M-TAC &middot; CARS</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Scenario-based training through illustration</h4><p>Two-part toolkit: visual scenario centering lived experience + didactic strategies handout. Production went from rough sketch to final color through multiple review rounds.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Crisis Response</span><span class="cs-tag">Psychosis</span><span class="cs-tag">Training Tool</span></div><div class="cs-impact"><div class="il">Impact</div><p>Free, publicly available for supervision, team huddles, and trainings.</p></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://camobilecrisis.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Responding-to-Psychosis-TTA-Tool.pdf" class="btn btn-sm">View Toolkit (PDF) &rarr;</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-dark"><div class="med-tag">Documentary</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Rebuilding Butte</h3><div class="cl">Tiny Pine Foundation</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>From devastation to community healing</h4><p>25-minute documentary following the 2018 Camp Fire. Alyssa taught herself to build from YouTube and now leads other survivors. The build site became its own healing community.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Collective Trauma</span><span class="cs-tag">Housing</span><span class="cs-tag">Fundraising</span></div><div class="cs-impact"><div class="il">Impact</div><p>Continues to raise money for tiny homes. Model for disaster recovery.</p></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://youtu.be/fHQH2uz-Reg" class="btn btn-sm">Watch Film &rarr;</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-blue"><div class="med-tag">Animation</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Peer Support<br>Animated Films</h3><div class="cl">Lipp Studios</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Explaining peer support through metaphor</h4><p>Two-part series using an oversized map as metaphor. Flashlight imagery spotlights walking alongside someone. One film becomes hundreds of reusable assets.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Peer Support</span><span class="cs-tag">Youth</span><span class="cs-tag">Parent Specialists</span></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-gold"><div class="med-tag">Documentary</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>Olivia &amp; Rigo<br>Recreation Therapy</h3><div class="cl">Lipp Studios</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Film as a policy advocacy tool</h4><p>Documentary about Olivia (recreation therapist) and Rigo (TBI survivor). Goal: influence policymakers for RT licensure. Later used at a healthcare conference to convince insurers.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Policy Advocacy</span><span class="cs-tag">TBI</span><span class="cs-tag">Licensure</span></div><div class="cs-links"><a href="https://youtu.be/ceqZNZbwRV8" class="btn btn-sm">Watch Film &rarr;</a></div></div></div></div>

    <div class="c-slide"><div class="cs-layout"><div class="cs-vis bg-burgundy"><div class="med-tag">Illustration</div><div class="img-ph"></div><h3>The UPSIDE Story<br>Youth Advocacy</h3><div class="cl">CARS &middot; SAMHSA</div></div><div class="cs-body"><h4>Color psychology meets youth advocacy</h4><p>Illustrated comic toolkit using a muted blue palette: blue conveys melancholy but also hope. Features different perspectives of scenes: lights on vs. off, audience reactions, stage views.</p><div class="cs-tags"><span class="cs-tag">Youth Advocacy</span><span class="cs-tag">Color Psychology</span><span class="cs-tag">Comic Format</span></div></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>



