<!-- ═══════════ FRAMEWORK ═══════════ -->
<section id="framework" class="section section-white"><div class="section-inner">
  <span class="eyebrow">Our Approach</span>
  <h2 class="section-title">A Framework for Mental Health <span class="crayon-hl">Storytelling</span></h2>
  <p class="section-subtitle">Storytelling becomes the bridge between knowledge and action.</p>
  <div class="fw-visual">
    <div class="fw-col k"><h3>Knowledge or Practice</h3><div class="sub">What are we communicating?</div><ul><li>Evidence-based practice</li><li>Community-defined practice</li><li>Policy communication</li><li>Awareness campaign</li><li>Recovery principles</li></ul></div>
    <div class="fw-bridge"><div class="arr">&rarr;</div><div class="lbl">Storytelling Bridge</div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div></div>
    <div class="fw-col o"><h3>Intended Outcome</h3><div class="sub">What is the goal?</div><ul><li>Clinician adoption of training</li><li>Increase referrals</li><li>Influence policy</li><li>Shift attitudes or norms</li><li>Raise money</li></ul></div>
  </div>
  <div class="fw-med"><div class="la">The HOW</div><p>Documentary &middot; Animation &middot; Illustration &middot; Entertainment-Education &middot; Contact-Based Stigma</p></div>
  <div class="accordion" style="margin-top:40px">
    <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header">Why Digital Storytelling for Mental Health?<span class="ai-icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-body"><div class="abi"><p>Google processes 8.5+ billion searches/day. YouTube is the 2nd largest search engine. Storytelling content generates 2&ndash;3x higher engagement. People are 22x more likely to remember a fact wrapped in a story.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header">Intersecting Fields &amp; Academic Frameworks<span class="ai-icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-body"><div class="abi"><p>Implementation Science, Public Health Communication, Advocacy, Dissemination Science. Key frameworks: Knowledge-to-Action, Entertainment-Education (Moyer-Gus&eacute;), Transportation Theory (Green &amp; Brock, 2000).</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header">Dissemination: Going Beyond the Film<span class="ai-icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-body"><div class="abi"><p>One film becomes hundreds of assets: stills, snippets, posters, social posts, conference tools, grant evidence, and fundraising materials across training platforms, digital ads, publications, and physical materials.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="gold-strip"><p>&ldquo;How the film is created is <span class="crayon-hl crayon-hl-strong">more important</span> than the finished product.&rdquo; &mdash; Kay Lipp</p></div>

<!-- ═══════════ APPROACH ═══════════ -->
<section id="approach" class="section section-dark"><div class="section-inner">
  <span class="eyebrow">How We Work</span>
  <h2 class="section-title">Trauma-Informed &amp; Ethical Storytelling</h2>
  <p class="section-subtitle">We stand by everything we make.</p>
  <div class="principles-grid">
    <div class="pc"><h3>Recovery-Oriented</h3><p>Every production centers hope, agency, and wholeness. We create with people, not about them.</p></div>
    <div class="pc"><h3>Strategic Sharing</h3><p>Participants maintain ownership and can request changes or deletion. Psychological safety first.</p></div>
    <div class="pc"><h3>Co-Directorship</h3><p>The storyteller holds the power. They review every iteration and co-create the narrative.</p></div>
    <div class="pc"><h3>Crisis Protocols</h3><p>Care teams available for debrief. We plan for what can come up during production.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="accordion" style="margin-top:40px">
    <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header">What is Strategic Sharing?<span class="ai-icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-body"><div class="abi"><p>Coined by the Foster Care Alumni Network in the 1990s. Provides education around sharing stories in ways that create impact while remaining psychologically safe for the storyteller.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="accordion-item"><button class="accordion-header">How Does Co-Directorship Work?<span class="ai-icon">+</span></button><div class="accordion-body"><div class="abi"><p>For OnTrack NY, Kay showed each subject footage after every shot. For Stanford INSPIRE animation, the team collaborated with clinicians and people with lived experience throughout every stage.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>



